</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Brady</surname><given-names>PC</given-names></name><name><surname>Burkhart</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The double-pulley technique for double-row rotator cuff repair</article-title><source>Arthroscopy</source><year>2007</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>675 e1</fpage><lpage>4</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17560485</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lo</surname><given-names>IK</given-names></name><name><surname>Burkhart</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Transtendon arthroscopic repair of partial-thickness, articular surface tears of the rotator cuff</article-title><source>Arthroscopy</source><year>2004</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>214</fpage><lpage>220</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14760358</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Park</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><name><surname>Tibone</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Elattrache</surname><given-names>NS</given-names></name><name><surname>Ahmad</surname><given-names>CS</given-names></name><name><surname>Jun</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>TQ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Part II: Biomechanical assessment for a footprint-restoring transosseous-equivalent rotator cuff repair technique compared with a double-row repair technique</article-title><source>J Shoulder Elbow Surg</source><year>2007</year></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Park</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><name><surname>Elattrache</surname><given-names>NS</given-names></name><name><surname>Ahmad</surname><given-name